# Frontend UI/UX — Mandatory Standards

**Full guide:** `docs/FRONTEND-UI-UX-STANDARDS.md` — read and follow it on every frontend change.

## Stack
Blade + Livewire Volt + Flux + Tailwind + Alpine. No new CSS frameworks or jQuery.

## Non-negotiables
1. **Mobile-first responsive** — base styles first, then `sm:`/`md:`/`lg:`. Test 320px–1440px. Min tap target 44px.
2. **Design tokens** — use `brand-*`, `shadow-elevation-*`, `rounded-md-*` from `tailwind.config.js`. No hardcoded hex in templates.
3. **Reuse components** — `x-primary-button`, `x-text-input`, `x-modal`, etc. before inline duplicates.
4. **All UI states** — loading (`wire:loading`), empty, error, success. Never ship happy-path only.
5. **Accessibility** — semantic HTML, `focus-visible:ring-*`, form labels, `aria-label` on icon buttons, WCAG AA contrast.
6. **Reactivity** — debounce search inputs; `wire:key` in loops; disable buttons while loading.
7. **Bengali-first UX** — natural copy, `bn()` for marketing numerals, layouts that fit longer strings.
8. **Performance** — lazy images, aspect ratios, paginate long lists, no inline `<style>`/`<script>`.

## Backend
**Do not change backend code.** See `.cursor/rules/no-backend-changes.mdc` — markup/styling only; preserve existing routes, logic, and behavior.

## Before completing any frontend task
Run through the checklist in `docs/FRONTEND-UI-UX-STANDARDS.md` §13.
